  "modifications": [
    "All relative TypeScript imports use .js specifiers for Node ESM and Archify self-analysis.",
    "parser/parser.ts: arithmetic-chain depth limit raised from 256 to 4096; Archify traverses such chains iteratively and does not run the recursive type evaluator.",
    "Parser and tokenizer return syntax nodes, tokens and line ranges. Parsing drops profiling, Notebook and stub-specific modes, editor formatting statistics, diagnostic suppression metadata, duplicate import and file indexes, and unused AST ownership and string-annotation tables. Syntax diagnostics and type-comment parsing are retained.",
    "common helpers retain parser-required assertions, ranges, diagnostic messages and token utilities. Editor APIs and type-checker diagnostics are excluded.",
    "localization/localize.ts and strings.ts retain only referenced English parser diagnostics; environment locale lookup and other analyzer/editor strings are excluded. strings.ts is the filtered JSON data expressed as a TypeScript constant.",
    "parser/stringVersionChecks.ts adapts only pre-3.12 f-string syntax checks from checker.ts visitStringList, using the parser diagnostic sink instead of a type evaluator.",
    "No upstream CLI, LSP, Program, binder, type evaluator, typeshed or target-code execution is included."
  ]
}
